Package: com.kern0x1b.telegramd
Name: Telegram relaunch daemon
Architecture: iphoneos-arm
Maintainer: kern0x1b <kern0x1b@users.noreply.github.com>
Author: kern0x1b <kern0x1b@users.noreply.github.com>
Section: System
Priority: optional
Depends: firmware (>= 6.0), firmware (<< 7.0)
Description: keeps Telegram running in the background after a force-quit or a jetsam kill
 A small root LaunchDaemon that checks every 30 seconds whether the Telegram
 process exists and, when it does not, asks SpringBoard to launch it suspended
 into the background. Nothing is hooked or injected, and all Telegram work
 stays inside the app. Creating
 /var/mobile/Library/Preferences/com.kern0x1b.telegram.nolaunch stops the
 relaunching without uninstalling.
